            <ArticleTitle>[Splenosis: an unrecognized cause of pelvic pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>335-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of painful pelvic splenosis is reported. This diagnosis concerns a patient suffering from pelvic pain who had had a splenectomy done thirteen years earlier. Two complementary examinations allowed us to make a precise pre-operatory diagnosis. The differential diagnoses are listed and endometriosis in particular. The authors think that the nodules of splenosis are probably a defense against infections affecting &quot;splenic&quot; patients. Consequently, the removal only of symptomatic ectopic splenic tissue is indicated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
